# Space profile invariants

The space profile is selected via `cmake -DTETHYS_PROFILE=space`. Code under `slave/src/profiles/space/**` and `slave/profiles/space.cmake` must uphold every invariant below.

## Invariants (parent plan section 3.3)

| Concern | Invariant |
| --- | --- |
| Transports | UART/SxI wrapped in CCSDS COP-1 + CAN (1-wire fault-tolerant). No raw UART. |
| Endianness | Fixed at compile time (per mission target). |
| CAL page integrity | Mandatory EDAC (SEC-DED Hamming) wrapper on RAM. Flash mirror page mandatory. |
| Watchdog | Mandatory kick on DAQ tick. XCP must never block the watchdog path. |
| Seed-and-key | Mandatory, 16-byte AES-128 derived (ADR-0006). |
| Flight-mode default | DAQ disabled. Enable only via authenticated service-mode command (60s inactivity timeout). |
| STIM | Service-mode only. AES-128 unlock required. Whitelist still applies even in service mode. |
| A2L hash | Signed binary hash in A2L header; CONNECT refused on mismatch. |
| Logging | Budgeted ring buffer with watermark. No unbounded MDF4. |
| Coding rules | MISRA C:2023 mandatory + required + advisory. **No recursion.** **No goto.** All loops bounded. |
| Standards trace | ECSS-E-ST-40C Rev.1, ECSS-Q-ST-80C, NPR 7150.2D, NASA-STD-8739.8, DO-178C DAL-B, CCSDS 232.1-B-2 (COP-1), CCSDS 132.0-B-3 (TM). See standards matrix S10/S14/S16-S20/S32/S33. |

## Loss budget rows (from ADR-0010 draft)

Space rows: 8-11. CTO over COP-1 AD ≤ 1e-12/frame post-ARQ; CAN(1-wire FT) ≤ 1e-9/frame with mandatory EDAC.

## Banned

- Dynamic allocation (covered by `no-dynamic-allocation` rule but doubly banned here).
- Recursion, `goto`, unbounded loops (covered by `no-recursion-no-goto` rule).
- DAQ-on-by-default at flight time. Always require service-mode unlock.
- Plaintext seed-and-key. Always 16-byte AES-128 (ADR-0006).
